[13.198749, "o", "Warning: running headless with --yolo / approval-mode=yolo and no sandbox. All tool calls (shell, write, edit) auto-execute at this process's privilege level. Configure tools.executionSandbox on Linux or a supported legacy sandbox via --sandbox / QWEN_SANDBOX, or set QWEN_CODE_SUPPRESS_YOLO_WARNING=1 to silence this notice.\r\n"]
[264.288449, "o", "Done. All seven steps completed and verified.\r\n\r\n## What was built\r\n\r\n| Step | Result |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| 1–2 | Downloaded `FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base` and the LoRA adapter via `snapshot_download` |\r\n| 3 | Base configured as `XLMRobertaForSequenceClassification` with **20** labels (`ignore_mismatched_sizes=True`), `id2label`/`label2id` taken from the adapter's `config.json` so class indexing matches training |\r\n| 4 | Saved to `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base` (config, safetensors, tokenizer.json + sentencepiece vocab) |\r\n| 5 | `PeftModel.from_pretrained(...)` — adapter uses `modules_to_save: [\"classifier\"]`, so the trained head (`dense` 768×768, `out_proj` 20×768) is restored, not random |\r\n| 6 | `merge_and_unload()` → `/app/merged_model` (self-contained, no `lora` keys remain) |\r\n| 7 | `/app/detection_results.json` (10 entries, schema-validated) |\r\n\r\nKey detail: the adapter's `adapter_model.bin` carries the entire fine-tuned classification head. `build_model.py` asserts `torch.equal` between the adapt"]
[264.288481, "o", "er's `classifier.out_proj.weight` and the head in the PEFT model and again after merging, so a random-head silent failure can't slip through.\r\n\r\n## Detection results (argmax of logits)\r\n\r\n```\r\n 6  fr  0.9753  Bonjour, comment allez-vous aujourd'hui?\r\n 5  es  0.9890  Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy?\r\n 2  de  0.9973  Guten Tag, wie geht es Ihnen?\r\n 8  it  0.9888  Ciao, come stai oggi?\r\n12  pt  0.9896  Olá, como você está?\r\n13  ru  0.9856  Привет, как дела?\r\n 9  ja  0.9649  こんにちは、お元気ですか？\r\n19  zh  0.9360  你好，你好吗？\r\n 0  ar  0.9880  مرحبا، كيف حالك؟\r\n 4  en  0.9737  Hello, how are you?\r\n```\r\n\r\n10/10 distinct classes, mean confidence 0.979.\r\n\r\n## Verification beyond the seed samples\r\n\r\nLoaded the **saved merged model fresh** (not the in-memory object) and ran one unseen sentence in each of the 20 languages: **20/20 correct**, confidences 0.90–0.999, lowest on Thai (0.901). Both tokenizer classes (`XLMRobertaTokenizer` and the fast variant) load from bot"]
[264.288486, "o", "h output directories.\r\n\r\nFiles: `build_model.py`, `detect.py`, `detection_results.json`, plus the two model directories. Note this environment had no Python ML packages, so I installed CPU-only `torch` 2.15, `transformers` 5.22.1, `peft` 0.21.2 into the system Python — flagging that since it mutates the global environment rather than a venv.\r\n"]
[264.395903, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@3d92b1b29636:/app# "]
